@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
allowmixing
hide circle
hide empty methods
title G2 · Package structure: public roots and their dependencies
top to bottom direction
folder "AIL package\nComplete contract for a declared subset" as pkg #E8F3EB {
  class "surface\nCoverage claim" as surface {
    API subset and release
  }
  class "exports\nPublic roots" as roots {
    Named declarations
  }
  class "Private support\nReferenced declarations" as support {
    Authoritative even when not exported
  }
  class "environment\nExact configurations" as env {
    target + platform
    optional refinements
  }
  class "Dependency selections\nExact pins" as pins {
    Imports and catalogue aliases
  }
  surface --> roots : states the scope of
  roots --> support : references, possibly transitively
  roots --> env : names availability\nwhere applicable
  support --> env : covers each referencing\nuse where applicable
  env -[hidden]down-> pins
}
$package(imports, "Imported packages\nName, version, document digest")
$catalogue(catalogues, "Profile and ABI entries\nIdentifier, version, manifest digest")
pins --> imports : imports when needed
pins --> catalogues : selects definitions
legend bottom
  Schematic, not a fourth fixture package. Non-normative: L2–L3, A1.
  Dependency closure follows references from roots through support and pinned dependencies.
  Dependency membership does not confer export membership.
  Folder = package; cylinder = catalogue; compartmented box = contract item.
  Containment groups local items; labelled arrows show references or scope, not calls.
  Pins must resolve in an explicitly supplied resolution set. Internal clauses omitted.
endlegend
@enduml
